- -- WHAT IS IT ? -- -

	FirstLook allows your Users to have a first Look at today's new
	files.

	Shown is the number of files and the megs uploaded today and
	yesterday, furthermore the names of the files uploaded today - of
	course this all for sysop-definable subboards seperately.

	In other words, it was inspired by Calypso's QuickNew for S!X.

	Take a Look at "FirstLook.pic" to get an idea what it's for.


- -- HOW TO INSTALL ? -- -

	Move FirstLook, FirstLookAdder and FirstLook.dat to your PFiles:
	directory and add the following to line 499 of your bbstext:

	<CTRL-Q>#3PFiles:FirstLookAdder}

	Next run CNet's configuration program and go to the Events section.
	Add this:

	Command : RunCNetC
	Args    : pfiles:FirstLook -r
	Type    : Immediate--system idle or not
	Days    : Sat Sun Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri
	Time    : 2415 (would be 0:15am) or whenever you want
	Valid   : 100
	Interval: 0
	Iterate : 1

	Now edit "FirstLook.dat". It's structure is as follows:

	Line 1: ID string "FIRSTLOOK" (without ""'s; don't change!)
	Line 2: number of subboards to monitor
	      : the names of the subboards to monitor (EXACT!)
	      : 2 lines per subboard: today's files and bytes uploaded
	      : 2 lines per subboard: yesterday's files and bytes uploaded
	      : x lines with uploaded files per subboard where x depends on
	        the number of files uploaded to that subboard

	Here's an example (ignore comments):

	-8<-cut here------------------------------------------------------
	FIRSTLOOK		<- identifier string
	1			<- number of subboards
	Amiga Uploads	<- exact name of subboard
	2			<- today's files u/l'ed in this sub
	4452			<- today's bytes u/l'ed in this sub
	0			<- yesterday's files u/l'ed in this sub
	0			<- yesterday's bytes u/l'ed in this sub
	test.txt		<- names of files u/l'ed today in
	test2.txt		<- this subboard
	-8<-cut here------------------------------------------------------

	In order to add a new subboard "PC Uploads" it could look like
	this:

	-8<-cut here------------------------------------------------------
	FIRSTLOOK
	2
	Amiga Uploads
	PC Uploads	<- new subboard
	2
	4452
	1			<- today's files u/l'ed in 2nd sub
	723712		<- today's bytes u/l'ed in 2nd sub
	0			<- yesterday's values for 1st sub
	0			<- slided 2 lines down
	0
	0
	test.txt		<- 1st sub filenames
	test2.txt
	pacman.arj	<- 2nd sub filenames
	-8<-cut here------------------------------------------------------

	Of course this would be a datafile already in use. As you install
	it for the first time it would have to look like this:

	-8<-cut here------------------------------------------------------
	FIRSTLOOK
	2
	Amiga Uploads
	PC Uploads
	0
	0
	0
	0
	0
	0
	0
	0
	-8<-cut here------------------------------------------------------

	Got it? It's really quite simple. Note that FirstLook only checks
	for the ID line, but NOT for forgotten lines! So you might
	encounter corrupt values if you forget a line or two.

	Finally you may now wish to add FirstLook to your sys.welcome file.
	Of course you can also run it out of any other place, the PFiles:
	section, as a command...

	If you have some kind of maintenance section you may also want to
	add FirstLook with argument -r in order to be able to reset the
	datafile manually. Don't forget to restrict access.

	Example bbsmenu file for the beginners:

	-8<-cut here------------------------------------------------------
	1; Maintenance menu
		VF, VIEW Feedback
		VN, VIEW New
		EA, Edit Account
		EG, Edit Group
		WF, Write File
		RF, Read File
		AM, Activity Monitor
		LC, Call Log
		LU, Transfer Log
		DUmp
		LA, Amaint Log
		RUN
		DD, Download Direct
		*D
		FL, First Look |#2PFiles:FirstLook}
		FLR, First Look Reset |#3PFiles:FirstLook -r}

	2; Available everywhere

		[to be continued...]
	-8<-cut here------------------------------------------------------

	A common mistake: the | is followed by a Control-Q character, which
	is DISPLAYED as a { when editing in CNet's editors, but is NOT the
	{ char! It is by the way the MCI command introducer.

	That's for the installation!


- -- BUGS -- -

	This version should finally (grrr!) be bug-free, anyway if you find
	some bugs don't hesitate to contact me. Noone did with v1.0, seems
	nobody's using it ?!

	For the advanced/experienced sysops:
	There might be problems when several ports run FirstLookAdder at
	the same time. With the #3 call it's called exclusively by one port
	at a time but I could not test whether CNet forces the other ports
	to wait or whether it skips the PFiles. If so, the users can still
	run the Adder afterwards just by re-describing the file: it will be
	added then. Also when FirstLook resets its datafile (argument -r)
	it needs exclusive access to the datafile.


- -- IMPROVEMENTS & UPDATES -- -

	The next version will have a built-in configuration editor - for
	those being unable to understand the config structure :).

	I'll then probably also have added more multi-node compatibility.
	Let's see what the testing shows - IF it shows, which depends on YOU!
	I need YOUR comments, suggestions, bug reports etc.!

	Please upload the archive to AmiNet's comm/cnet directory. A .readme
	file is included. This allows other sysops to get new versions through
	one of the biggest distributions channels available. You know you'll
	benefit from it!

	Updates are available at the Indians Home BBS (see below), at Future
	World, of course at Black Moon, the Logic WHQ and on various other
	boards. And - I hope - also from AmiNet's comm/cnet directory.


